# ============================================================================
# Everything ignored here is either GENERATED by a build/test run or DOWNLOADED
# by a script — nothing in these paths is ever the only copy of anything.
# If a new tool starts writing into the repo, add its output here first.
#
# Companion file: .gitattributes decides LINE ENDINGS for everything that IS
# tracked. The two are easy to confuse — this file answers "does it go in?",
# that one answers "what does it look like when it comes out?".
# ============================================================================

# Build outputs
bin/
obj/
publish/
artifacts/
build/installer/Output/
*.binlog

# Fetched tools (re-fetched by build/fetch-ffmpeg.ps1 and build/make-installer.ps1;
# pinned by ffmpeg.lock.json, so the binaries themselves stay out of the repo).
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and it matters. Unanchored, `tools/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth — which silently swallowed
# build/tools/normalise-line-endings.ps1, a maintenance script the developer guide
# tells people to run. It existed on the machine that wrote it and on no other, and
# nothing complained, because ignoring a file it was never asked to track is git
# doing exactly its job. Only the fetched binaries live at the root; anything under
# build/ is source.
/tools/

# Test working folders and coverage output
TestResults/
coverage/
coveragereport/
*.received.*
*.trx
*.coverage

# Local logs and crash dumps from running the app or ffmpeg out of the tree
*.log
*.dmp

# Recorded footage — always generated, never source. A stray trial or test
# recording must not end up in history (video files are also far too big for it).
*.mkv
*.mp4

# User/IDE files
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.DotSettings.user

# Merge and rebase litter. Committing a .orig is harmless but confusing; a
# committed .rej is a half-applied patch masquerading as source.
*.orig
*.rej

# Windows Explorer litter
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# macOS litter (checkouts on a Mac for docs work happen)
.DS_Store

# Local secrets must never be committed (signing certs are provided via
# environment variables — see build/sign.ps1)
*.pfx
*.snk
